.TH ZLINE 1 "September 2026" "zline 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zline \- fast, modern, and flexible pure-Zsh prompt engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zline
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B zline preset
\fIPRESET\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...]
.br
.B zline style
\fISTYLE\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...]
.br
.B zline init
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBzline\fR is an ultra-fast, modern, and flexible pure-Zsh prompt engine designed as a streamlined replacement for Powerlevel10k.
It delivers sub-millisecond synchronous rendering (< 0.7 ms) with zero subprocess forks on the critical prompt path,
relying exclusively on native Zsh parameter expansions, built-in modules, and an event-driven architecture.
.PP
Heavy background operations (such as full Git working tree status) are computed asynchronously
via non-blocking pipes and ZLE file descriptor handlers (\fBzle -F\fR), ensuring the interactive shell
never stutters or drops user keystrokes.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration in \fBzline\fR is declarative and concise, avoiding the need for hundreds of global environment variables.
Prompts are defined using standard Zsh arrays. Array elements do not require quotes unless an argument contains whitespace or an explicit empty string:
.RS
.nf
# Set visual preset and global flags
zline preset pure --transient --no-icons

# Define left prompt segments (unquoted)
zline_left=(
  dir --shorten 1 --anchor git
  git --clean 2 --dirty 3
  rust
  package
  newline
  prompt_char
)

# Define right prompt segments (unquoted)
zline_right=(
  exec_time --min 2
  time --color cyan
)

# Initialize prompt engine
zline init
.fi
.RE

.SH PRESETS
\fBzline\fR includes four built-in presets:
.TP
.B powerline
Classic multi-colored background blocks joined by Powerline arrow glyphs (U+E0B0, U+E0B2).
.TP
.B lean
Modern, flat, space-separated layout with crisp foreground colors.
.TP
.B rainbow
High-contrast, vivid powerline blocks designed for rapid visual parsing.
.TP
.B pure
Minimalist two-line prompt inspired by Sindre Sorhus's Pure prompt.
.TP
.B catppuccin
Pastel Mocha palette with lavender and sapphire accents.
.TP
.B tokyonight
Tokyo Night Storm palette with deep blue and bright cyan accents.
.TP
.B nord
Arctic frost palette with polar night and snow storm colors.
.TP
.B gruvbox
Retro groove warm palette with aqua, yellow, and faded orange.

.SH BUILT-IN SEGMENTS
.TP
.B dir
Displays current working directory.
.RS
.IP "\fB--shorten\fR \fIN\fR"
Shortens intermediate directory components to \fIN\fR characters (e.g. \fB--shorten 1\fR produces \fB~/s/g/c/zline\fR).
.IP "\fB--keep-last\fR \fIN\fR"
Number of trailing directory components to keep full (default: 1).
.IP "\fB--alias\fR \fIpattern=replacement\fR"
Substitutes matching path components (e.g. \fB--alias github.com=gith\fR).
.IP "\fB--anchor\fR \fIgit\fR | \fIproject\fR"
Anchors at Git repository root or project root, shortening paths above the repository but keeping the project name full.
.IP "\fB--last\fR \fIN\fR"
Truncates path to the last \fIN\fR directory components (e.g. \fB--last 2\fR produces \fB.../parent/current\fR).
.IP "\fB--format\fR \fIfunc_name\fR"
Delegates path formatting to a custom Zsh function setting \fB$REPLY\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B git
Fast Git status segment.
.RS
.IP "\fB--clean\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color used when working tree is clean (default: 2 / green).
.IP "\fB--dirty\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color used when working tree has changes (default: 3 / yellow).
.IP "\fB--ahead\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color used when branch is ahead of remote (default: 12 / bright-blue).
.IP "\fB--staged-icon\fR \fIsym\fR, \fB--unstaged-icon\fR \fIsym\fR, \fB--untracked-icon\fR \fIsym\fR"
Custom status glyphs for git state counters (default: \fB+\fR, \fB!\fR, \fB?\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B status
Command exit status indicator.
.RS
.IP "\fB--hide-zero\fR"
Hides status badge when command succeeded (exit code 0).
.IP "\fB--show-zero\fR"
Displays 0 in green when command succeeded.
.RE
.TP
.B exec_time
Execution duration for previous command.
.RS
.IP "\fB--min\fR \fIN\fR"
Minimum duration in seconds before displaying execution time (default: 2).
.RE
.TP
.B prompt_char
Active prompt symbol.
.RS
.IP "\fB--symbol\fR \fIsym\fR"
Character to display (default: ❯).
.IP "\fB--root\fR \fIsym\fR"
Character to display for root user (default: #).
.IP "\fB--error\fR \fIcolor\fR"
Color to display when previous command failed (default: 9 / bright-red).
.RE
