.SH COLOR PALETTE
\fBzline\fR standardizes on Base16 / Term16 colors (0\(en15) to guarantee seamless harmony with any terminal color scheme:
.IP "0 / 8"
black / bright-black (grey)
.IP "1 / 9"
red / bright-red (errors, root)
.IP "2 / 10"
green / bright-green (clean git, success)
.IP "3 / 11"
yellow / bright-yellow (dirty git, warnings)
.IP "4 / 12"
blue / bright-blue (directory, branch)
.IP "5 / 13"
magenta / bright-magenta (language runtimes)
.IP "6 / 14"
cyan / bright-cyan (cloud environments)
.IP "7 / 15"
white / bright-white (primary prompt symbol)

.SH MODERN TERMINAL PROTOCOLS
\fBzline\fR natively integrates modern terminal standards:
.TP
.B OSC 133
Semantic shell integration markings (prompt start, command start, command output, return code) for Ghostty, Kitty, WezTerm, iTerm2, and VS Code.
.TP
.B OSC 7
Current working directory reporting for automatic directory inheritance across tabs and splits.
.TP
.B OSC 8
Terminal hyperlinks for clickable file paths and Git repositories.
.SH UNIVERSAL SEGMENT FLAGS
Every segment in \fBzline\fR universally supports the following command-line flags:
.TP
.B \-\-icon \fIsymbol\fR
Overrides the segment default icon with a custom glyph (e.g. \fB\-\-icon " "\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-icon ""
Suppresses the icon for this specific segment, rendering only the text/content without an icon or leading spacer.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIcode\fR | \-\-fg \fIcode\fR
Sets the foreground text and icon color (Base16 index 0\(en15, semantic color name e.g. \fBcyan\fR, 256-color index, or hex \fB#RRGGBB\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-bg \fIcode\fR
Sets the background block color in Powerline and Rainbow visual styles.
.TP
.B \-\-prefix \fIstring\fR
Prepends an arbitrary string before segment content.
.TP
.B \-\-suffix \fIstring\fR
Appends an arbitrary string after segment content.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIfunction\fR
Post-processes segment content with a custom Zsh function setting \fB$REPLY\fR.

.SH GLOBAL STYLE FLAGS
Global prompt behavior is configured via flags on \fBzline preset\fR or \fBzline style\fR:
.TP
.B \-\-transient
Automatically collapses multi-line prompts down to a minimal \fB❯\fR symbol on Enter.
.TP
.B \-\-transient\-dir
Retains directory path in collapsed transient prompt instead of symbol-only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-transient
Disables transient prompt collapse.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-icons
Suppresses default segment icons globally across all segments (pure text mode).
.TP
.B \-\-icons
Enables default segment icons (default).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-osc
Disables OSC 133 (semantic shell integration) and OSC 7 (working directory) escape codes.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Replaces all Nerd Font symbols and Powerline glyphs with pure ASCII text fallbacks.
.TP
.B \-\-nerdfont
Enables Nerd Font v3 and Powerline symbols (default).
.TP
.B \-\-frame \fIstyle\fR
Selects corner frame connector layout: \fBnone\fR, \fBleft\fR, or \fBfull\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-frame\-shape \fIshape\fR
Selects frame corner glyph style: \fBrounded\fR (╭─), \fBsharp\fR (┌─), or \fBdouble\fR (╔═).
.TP
.B \-\-connect \fIstyle\fR
Draws connecting line between left and right prompts on multiline layouts: \fBsolid\fR (─), \fBdashed\fR (┄), \fBdotted\fR (┈), or custom character.
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-color \fIcode\fR
Sets connecting line color (default: 8 / grey).
.TP
.B \-\-rprompt\-line \fI1|2\fR
Embeds right prompt into line 1 via connecting line or keeps native right prompt on the command input line.
.TP
.B \-\-title
Automatically updates terminal window and tab titles with current directory and running commands.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-title
Disables terminal window and tab title updates.
.TP
.B \-\-notify [\fIseconds\fR]
Enables desktop notifications via OSC 777 / OSC 9 when commands exceed duration threshold (default: 30s).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Disables desktop notifications.
.TP
.B \-\-hyperlinks
Formats directory paths and Git repositories as clickable OSC 8 terminal hyperlinks.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hyperlinks
Disables clickable OSC 8 hyperlinks.

.SH CLI COMMANDS
.TP
\fBzline preset\fR \fIname\fR [\fIoptions...\fR]
Loads a preset theme configuration.
.TP
\fBzline preset list\fR
Lists all available presets and curated themes.
.TP
\fBzline preset show\fR \fIname\fR
Displays configuration source of specified preset.
.TP
\fBzline style\fR \fIname\fR [\fIoptions...\fR]
Configures visual styling (\fB--transient\fR, \fB--transient-dir\fR, \fB--ascii\fR, \fB--no-icons\fR, \fB--no-osc\fR, \fB--notify\fR).
.TP
\fBzline init\fR
Compiles segments and initializes hooks.
.TP
\fBzline bench\fR [\fB--profile\fR] [\fIiterations\fR]
Runs execution latency benchmark or segment micro-profiling over \fIiterations\fR (default: 1000).
.TP
\fBzline version\fR
Prints active version.
.TP
\fBzline doctor\fR
Runs comprehensive health and environment diagnostics.
.TP
\fBzline configure\fR [\fIoptions...\fR]
Interactive setup wizard and config generator.
.TP
\fBzline compile\fR
Pre-compiles scripts to memory-mapped Zsh wordcode (.zwc).
.TP
\fBzline clean\fR
Removes compiled .zwc wordcode files.
.TP
\fBzline migrate\fR [\fIp10k_file\fR] [\fIoutput_file\fR]
Automatically translates Powerlevel10k configuration to zline.
.TP
\fBzline compare\fR
Runs performance comparison benchmark against other prompt architectures.
.TP
\fBzline update\fR
Pulls the latest release and recompiles bytecode.
.TP
\fBzline notify\fR [\fIon\fR [\fIseconds\fR] | \fIoff\fR | \fIthreshold\fR \fIseconds\fR | \fIstatus\fR]
Configures long-running command desktop notifications via OSC 777 and OSC 9 escape sequences.

